1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,200
Count the beasts on an imperial roof.
{\fs13}I'm your China Travel Expert

2
00:00:02,200 --> 00:00:05,500
Every ridge caps at nine — except one.

3
00:00:05,500 --> 00:00:10,500
A saint leads the line, then the guardian beasts fall in behind.

4
00:00:10,500 --> 00:00:15,500
The more figures, the higher the building's rank.

5
00:00:15,500 --> 00:00:20,500
Nine is the ceiling everywhere in China — but here it hits ten.

6
00:00:20,500 --> 00:00:25,000
The tenth is the Hangshi, carved on no other roof.

7
00:00:25,000 --> 00:00:28,000
Only the Hall of Supreme Harmony — the emperor's throne hall — wears all ten.

8
00:00:28,000 --> 00:00:31,000
★ Expert Tip: at the Forbidden City, look up and count the corner beasts.

9
00:00:31,000 --> 00:00:34,000
Nine beasts or ten — which roof truly outranks the rest?
